#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:93
msgid ""
"mlockall failed: Cannot allocate memory\n"
"Couldn't lock all cached virtual memory.\n"
"Pagefaults from reading pages not yet mapped into RAM will be recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:99
msgid ""
"After the initialization stage of the demo program, it will attempt to lock "
"all cached memory into RAM and prevent future dynamic memory allocations "
"using ``mlockall``. This is to prevent pagefaults from loading lots of new "
"memory into RAM. (See `the realtime design article <https://design.ros2.org/"
"articles/realtime_background.html#memory-management>`__ for more "
"information.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:103
msgid ""
"The demo will continue on as usual when this occurs. You could also see the "
"output as following, that means the number of pagefaults encountered during "
"execution:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:108
msgid ""
"rttest statistics:\n"
"  - Minor pagefaults: 20\n"
"  - Major pagefaults: 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:112
msgid "If we want those pagefaults to go away, we'll have to..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:115
msgid "Adjust permissions for memory locking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:117
#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:213
msgid "Add to ``/etc/security/limits.conf`` (as sudo):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:121
msgid "<your username>    -   memlock   <limit in kB>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:123
msgid ""
"A limit of ``-1`` is unlimited. If you choose this, you may need to "
"accompany it with ``ulimit -l unlimited`` (as root) after editing the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:126
msgid ""
"After saving the file, log out and log back in. Then rerun the "
"``pendulum_demo`` invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/Motion-planning/Real-Time-Programming.rst:129
msgid ""
"You'll either see zero pagefaults in your output file, or an error saying "
"that a bad_alloc exception was caught. If this happened, you didn't have "
"enough free memory available to lock the memory allocated for the process "
"into RAM. You'll need to install more RAM in your computer to see zero "
"pagefaults!"
msgstr ""

